# Documented exceptions for the Trivy image scan.
#
# The gate blocks the build on fixable HIGH/CRITICAL findings. This file is the
# pressure valve for the rare case where a single finding is flagged but does
# not apply (false positive, an unused code path) or has to be accepted for a
# short, deliberate window.
#
# Rules:
#   - One vulnerability ID per line (e.g. CVE-2026-12345).
#   - Always add a comment with the reason and a review date.
#   - Keep it short. An entry that no longer applies gets removed.
#
# libpcre2-8-0 in the Debian 12 base of both images. The fix (10.42-1+deb12u2)
# is in bookworm-security, but python:3.12-slim-bookworm and node:24-slim have
# not been rebuilt on top of it yet. The flaw needs an attacker-supplied regular
# expression and the PCRE2 JIT API, and neither Python nor Node uses libpcre2
# for its own regex engine. Remove this entry once the base image digests in
# deploy/Dockerfile.backend and deploy/Dockerfile.frontend are bumped.
# Review by 2026-10-18.
CVE-2026-103111
